				<wikidot:authorName>Crayne</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1346995</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Only just saw moose's reply to my post on what number I'd like if my entry doesn't win. Sorry about that, and I agree that if this is something that is actually going to happen (granting numbers based on a reply here), saying 'anything under 2010' isn't very helpful.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Anyway, in that case: 2002 since that was the year I had in mind if 2000 fell through (it's the year my oldest son was born). If Reject enters, and his entry survives, I'll take 2004 (since Kalinin asked for 2003.)</span></p> <p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Okay, Reject didn't enter, and Kalinin missed this post when he edited on the 10th of December. However, his entry is far more highly rated than mine, so I'm inclined to let him take 2002. I'll gladly take 2003 (which he originally asked for).</span></p> <p>After conferring with Kalinin, I can have 2002. Thanks! I wonder how many more times I'll be editing this post. :P</p> <p>Also, question: how does the reposting work? Are we able to edit the pagename (not the title, but the name) or do we repost thereby blanking scores?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
